# Version control
#
# Six Dockerfiles here COPY the whole build context (the quicraft, etcd and
# dragonboat benchmark images and the three devcontainer images), so without
# this .git is baked into every one of them -- 9.7M of history in a 20M tree,
# and the complete commit history of a private repository inside images that
# may be published. Nothing in any build reads git metadata: there is no
# version stamping, and the only `git` in a Dockerfile is apt installing the
# client into the devcontainer.
.git/

# Build artifacts
build/coverage/
build/quicraft

# IDE and editor files
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test data (created by integration tests running as root in Docker)
**/data/
integration-test.log

# Rust build artifacts (openraft benchmark)
test/performance/openraft/target/

# Go workspace (breaks sub-module Docker builds)
go.work
go.work.sum

# Agent / AI context files
.claude/
.cursor/
.codex/

# Module credentials for the benchmark image builds (test/performance/README.md).
# Six Dockerfiles COPY the whole context, so without this line the token the
# BuildKit secret exists to keep out of every layer would be copied into every
# layer by the COPY that precedes the secret mount. .gitignore protects git
# only; this is the docker half, and test/buildgates pins the two together.
.devcontainer/.env
